WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:20.069
For many years, Hook and his pirates had searched for the hidden entrance to the Lost Boys' home, but had never found it.

2
00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:26.147
As the pirates followed the boys, hoping to be led to the entrance, they saw Tootles.

3
00:00:26.148 --> 00:00:33.957
As always, Tootles was way behind the other boys, who had already disappeared into their hiding place.

4
00:00:33.958 --> 00:00:38.529
The pirates were about to shoot him dead when Hook stopped them.

5
00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:44.764
"If you fire your pistols now," he roared, "the Indians will find us.

6
00:00:44.765 --> 00:00:47.770
Do you want to lose your hair?"

7
00:00:47.771 --> 00:00:54.566
Meanwhile, Tootles had disappeared, and the pirates began to run back to their ship in fear of the Indians.

8
00:00:54.567 --> 00:01:01.719
Alone with Smee, who had stayed behind, Hook calmed down and told his sad tale.

9
00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:06.033
"I want to catch all six boys at one time.

10
00:01:06.034 --> 00:01:10.503
But most of all I want their captain, Peter Pan.

11
00:01:10.504 --> 00:01:16.765
It was Peter Pan who cut off my hand." He shook his hook threateningly.

12
00:01:16.766 --> 00:01:20.620
"I've waited a long time to catch him with this."

13
00:01:20.621 --> 00:01:28.170
"I've heard you say many times," said Smee, "that one hook is worth a dozen hands."

14
00:01:28.171 --> 00:01:35.840
"Nonetheless, I want Peter. He flung my hand to a crocodile that was passing by.

15
00:01:35.841 --> 00:01:42.117
And the crocodile liked my hand so much that it has followed me ever since.

16
00:01:42.118 --> 00:01:49.951
On land and sea, it licks its lips, hoping for the rest of me. I can never relax."

17
00:01:49.952 --> 00:01:54.830
"In a way that's a compliment to you, Captain," said the loyal Smee.

18
00:01:54.831 --> 00:01:59.947
"It's Peter who gave the crocodile its taste for me," said Hook.

19
00:01:59.948 --> 00:02:09.091
"Luckily, that crocodile also swallowed a clock, so I always know by its ticking sound whenever it comes near.

20
00:02:09.092 --> 00:02:14.303
Without that warning, it would already have had me for supper."

21
00:02:14.304 --> 00:02:20.413
"Someday that clock will break down," said Smee, "and you'll be in big trouble."

22
00:02:20.414 --> 00:02:27.601
"Yes, that's my fear." Shuddering, Hook sat down on a giant mushroom for a moment.

23
00:02:27.602 --> 00:02:31.936
Suddenly he jumped up. "This seat is hot!"

24
00:02:31.937 --> 00:02:34.936
Hook and Smee examined the giant mushroom.

25
00:02:34.937 --> 00:02:39.958
When Smee tried to pull it out of the ground, he found it had no roots.

26
00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:43.520
Furthermore, it had smoke coming out of it.

27
00:02:43.521 --> 00:02:48.273
They had discovered the chimney of the Lost Boys' underground home.

28
00:02:48.274 --> 00:02:51.701
Now they could hear the boys' voices.

29
00:02:51.702 --> 00:02:56.903
Smee whispered, "Did you hear them say Peter Pan will be back soon?"

30
00:02:56.904 --> 00:03:03.406
"Good!" said Hook. "Let's return to the ship and think of a way to capture him."

31
00:03:03.407 --> 00:03:06.393
But before they left, they heard one more thing.

32
00:03:06.394 --> 00:03:12.194
Tick-tock, tick-tock, tick-tock.

33
00:03:12.195 --> 00:03:20.536
Hook gasped, "It's the crocodile!" and he ran away. Smee quickly followed.

34
00:03:20.537 --> 00:03:26.930
The boys had a clever way in and out of their underground home, and they used it to come out.

35
00:03:26.931 --> 00:03:32.943
Tootles, who had been hiding from the pirates in the woods, joined the rest of his friends.

36
00:03:32.944 --> 00:03:38.213
He was very excited. "I saw a wonderful thing in the sky!

37
00:03:38.214 --> 00:03:43.294
A great white bird! It's flying this way."

38
00:03:43.295 --> 00:03:47.109
"What kind of bird?" the others asked.

39
00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:53.731
"I don't know," replied Tootles, "but it looks almost like a girl.

40
00:03:53.732 --> 00:04:02.512
It flies as though it's in pain, and it keeps crying 'Poor Wendy'."

41
00:04:02.513 --> 00:04:05.584
"I remember now," said Slightly.

42
00:04:05.585 --> 00:04:09.765
"I think there are birds called the Wendy Bird."

43
00:04:09.766 --> 00:04:14.419
"Here it comes!" shouted Curly, pointing upward.

44
00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:19.719
They could hear Wendy's cries—along with the tinkle of Tinker Bell.

45
00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:24.541
With Peter far away, Tinker Bell didn't have to act nice anymore.

46
00:04:24.542 --> 00:04:26.564
She could do what she wanted.

47
00:04:26.565 --> 00:04:32.083
In the air, the jealous fairy had been pinching Wendy all over her body.

48
00:04:32.084 --> 00:04:34.966
Seeing the boys, she stopped.

49
00:04:34.967 --> 00:04:38.848
"Hello, Tink!" yelled the boys.

50
00:04:38.849 --> 00:04:41.807
Tinker Bell landed in a nearby tree.

51
00:04:41.808 --> 00:04:48.151
"Hello, boys. Peter wants you to shoot the Wendy Bird," she lied.

52
00:04:48.152 --> 00:04:54.370
Never one to question Peter's wishes, Tootles immediately aimed his bow and arrow.

53
00:04:54.371 --> 00:04:58.082
The others watched Wendy, who was still up in the sky.

54
00:04:58.083 --> 00:05:03.757
"Peter will be so proud of you!" Tinker Bell said encouragingly.

55
00:05:03.758 --> 00:05:13.365
Tootles fired, and Wendy fluttered to the ground, an arrow in her chest.
